    "long_instructions": "**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Call `train_test_split` to split your inputs and outputs into training inputs, test inputs, training outputs, and test outputs.\r\n2. Call `make_pipeline` to make a machine learning pipeline. Your pipeline should include a `StandardScaler` to scale your data and an `MLPClassifier` or `MLPRegressor` to use a neural network.\r\n3. Fit your neural network to the training data.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nTo use `scikit-learn` features, you’ll need to import them first with lines like:\r\n\r\n```\r\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\r\nfrom sklearn.neural_network import MLPClassifier\r\nfrom sklearn.neural_network import MLPRegressor\r\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline\r\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\r\n```\r\n\r\nAsk AI Tutor for help if you get stuck!\r\n",
